Here is a step-by-step guide to building a simple website using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript:

1. Create a new file in your preferred text editor (e.g. Notepad, Sublime Text, Atom) and save it with a .html extension.
2. In the file, add the basic structure of a web page using HTML tags. This includes the `<html>`, `<head>`, and `<body>` tags.
3. Inside the `<head>` tag, add the title of your website using the `<title>` tag.
4. Inside the `<body>` tag, add the content of your website using HTML tags such as `<p>` for paragraphs, `<a>` for links, and `<img>` for images.
5. To style your website, add CSS to the `<head>` tag using the `<style>` tag. You can also use CSS preprocessors like Sass or Less to make your code more organized.
6. To add interactivity to your website, add JavaScript to the `<body>` tag using the `<script>` tag. You can use libraries like jQuery or React to simplify your code.
7. Save and open your website in a web browser to test it.

